<title>UK: Jermyn venture buys Dublin shopping centre.</title>
<headline>Jermyn venture buys Dublin shopping centre.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jermyn Investment Properties said on Monday that its Irish based joint venture Castle Market Holdings had bought the Stillorgan Shopping Centre in Dublin from the Bank of Ireland pension fund for 45 million punts.  </p>
<p>Stillorgan was the first modern purpose-built shopping centre in Dublin and produces annual rents of over three million punts. Castle Market intends to expand the retailing area.</p>
<p>&quot;There is considerable potential in this high quality investment at a time when the retail environment in Ireland is developing at a rapid pace,&quot; said Juliet Cogswell, a director of Jermyn, in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
